Title: Interface in function declaration statement
Description: There is a interface like this:

``` ts
interface searchFunc {
    (source: string, subString: string): boolean;
}
```

I know I can use it in **function definition expression**:

``` ts
var mySearch: searchFunc = function(src, sub) {
    var result = src.search(sub);
    if (result == -1) {
        return false;
    }
    else {
        return true;
    }
}
```

But how can I use it in **function declaration statement** like below? Do I need to change the structure of interface?

``` ts
function mySearch(src, sub): searchFunc {
    var result = src.search(sub);
    if (result == -1) {
        return false;
    }
    else {
        return true;
    }
}
```

I'm waiting online,hope a answering.


